      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1ab02eab-1bef-4208-a026-3d438d9cb7df",
      "name": "search_documents",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.vectorStoreInMemory",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        480,
        944
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "retrieve-as-tool",
        "toolDescription": "Search the uploaded documents for passages relevant to the user question. Returns text chunks with metadata including document_name. Always call this before answering.",
        "memoryKey": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "rag_documents"
        },
        "topK": 5,
        "includeDocumentMetadata": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c28415de-d2db-4142-b4b3-c11e2d1c8d68",
      "name": "Note: Ingestion",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        -96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Part 1: Ingestion\nOpen the form, upload a PDF and submit.\n\n1. **Upload PDF** (Form Trigger) receives the file as binary data.\n2. **PDF Loader** extracts the text and tags each chunk with its `document_name` so answers can cite the source.\n3. **Split into Chunks** cuts the text into ~1000 character pieces with 200 overlap so context isn't lost at boundaries.\n4. **Store Chunks in Vector Store** embeds each chunk and saves it in the built-in Simple Vector Store under the key `rag_documents`.\n\nNote: the Simple Vector Store lives in n8n memory, so it is cleared on restart. Fine for demos; use Pinecone/Qdrant/Supabase for production.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 640
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "aebaaffc-de1a-4f8e-8636-1a8e05aaab86",
      "name": "Note: Chat",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Part 2: Chat\nOpen the chat and ask questions about your uploaded documents.\n\n1. **Chat with Documents** (Chat Trigger) receives each message.\n2. **RAG Agent** is told to answer ONLY from retrieved passages, cite the document name, and say \"I don't know\" when nothing relevant is found.\n3. **search_documents** is the vector store exposed as a retrieval tool. The agent calls it to fetch the top 5 matching chunks.\n4. **Conversation Memory** keeps the last 10 messages for follow-up questions.",
        "color": 5,
        "width": 784,
        "height": 432
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "dee9ea09-6c30-49aa-b065-b7532b9bd126",
      "name": "Note: Embeddings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        256,
        128
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Embeddings\nIngestion and retrieval share the same embeddings model and the same memory key (`rag_documents`). They must match exactly, otherwise similarity search returns nothing useful.",
        "color": 3,
        "width": 144,
        "height": 208
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d091c7e3-05fa-4ac4-b421-aa7c889787e2",
      "name": "Note: Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        144,
        1152
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# RAG: Chat with your documents\nA portfolio project showing Retrieval-Augmented Generation in n8n.\n\n**How to use**\n1. Run the **Upload PDF** form and submit one or more PDFs.\n2. Open the chat and ask a question.\n\nAnswers come only from your documents, with citations. Unknown answers return \"I don't know\".\n\n**Setup:** connect an OpenAI credential on the chat model and embeddings nodes.",
        "color": 6,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 340
      }
    }
  ],
